{"ok": true, "command": "retrieve", "result": {"stopping_reason": "BUDGET_EXHAUSTED_WITH_GAPS", "evidence": [{"id": "a5825dd584d1f9bcc50a5c99", "sha256": "0881af766de8c52f61d03f21a3e8a133d9725a33ced3b902990e6a9e4de90430", "path": "docs/research/W2-87-memory-measure.md", "start_line": 38, "end_line": 66, "text": "## 2. The stores' fingerprint\n\nOne set of stores, built once in the head clone at `cffef92c8534` and used by all three runs. They were built by the base's code (`gov-base`), not by the pinned gov (deviation 1, \u00a77), with embeddings, as `env -u PYTHONPATH -u GOV_TICKET flock /tmp/gov-os-rebuild.lock <gov-base> rebuild --json`, after the disk gate.\n\n| | The rebuild |\n|---|---|\n| Code | the base's, `df0782fa4c4e` (`gov-base`) |\n| Gate at the start: disk | 875 GiB and 65,160,169 inodes free |\n| End (UTC) | 21:20:11 on 2026-10-30 |\n| Exit code | 0 |\n| Stores (`lexical`, `semantic`, `codeintel`) | each `recreated` |\n| Embeddings | built (never `--no-embeddings`) |\n\n**The digest the rebuild records** (`result.digest`; `result.store.digest` is the same value, with no invalid entries):\n\n- the stores' fingerprint: `0b7e7d00c83f52f5cd6772c95eb1ac7637b83c081f192699a68bd13bd63a35c5`\n\nThis worktree's own rebuild at the same commit, by its own code, gave the same digest.\n\n**The sha256 of each store file after the rebuild:**\n\n| Store file | sha256 |\n|---|---|\n| `.gov-runtime/store.db` | `bdb4572966a45eccbbfa7119b406b9ddc8b43cee509a71c44cc13c4d2e5d9070` |\n| `.gov-runtime/codeintel/home/code.db` | `45073c6280bd8a7e32b3a054cbb0eeea3b91e5b8589cbcb11ee3ab7885a38c17` |\n| `.gov-runtime/codeintel/home/_config.db` | `6881a590e961b4c4faff0180c79e87d6af9c34a9367e12cf28bbe2dbc4028cf8` (the same as W2-61's) |\n\n**The pinned gov's rebuild, not used:** the pinned gov (`5c40122014da`) rebuilt the stores at `060e03ef57ea` with exit 0 and digest `522296ef1709a39100d8a8ce9ed9819bf1c548373c3f877d7fa1cc41361c6c2d`, but every retrieval from them refused with STORE_MISSING (deviation 1, \u00a77).\n\n", "chunk_id": "a5825dd584d1f9bcc50a5c99", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "67fc18abf5b06e08805c72fe", "sha256": "60dffd15bb86453f2fdbe5287ad85877e67f2d1d8a96ae9369db98552fe1f779", "path": "tests/acceptance/W1-10/README.md", "start_line": 31, "end_line": 57, "text": "## The public interface\n\nNo `gov` command belongs to this ticket: `src/gov/cli/**` is outside its `allowed_paths`, so the reserved\n`gov rebuild` stays `NOT_IMPLEMENTED` and its case in `tests/acceptance/W1-07/test_w1_07_registry.py` is unchanged.\nThe tests call two packages. The engineer builds to exactly this:\n\n**`gov.store`** (`src/gov/store/`)\n\n| Function | Returns |\n|---|---|\n| `load(root)` | Builds `<root>/.gov-runtime/store.db` (a SQLite database) from the git repository at `root`, replacing what an earlier load left. Returns a map with at least `digest` (the store's digest) and `invalid` (a list of `{\"path\", \"reason\"}`, one per record that could not be loaded; empty when there is none). |\n| `digest(root)` | The digest of the store at `root`: a sha256 in lower-case hex (64 characters) of the store's logical content. |\n\n**`gov.records`** (`src/gov/records/`), each reading the store that `load` wrote\n\n| Function | Returns |\n|---|---|\n| `records(root, type=None, status=None)` | A list of maps, one per record that matches every filter given, each with at least `id`, `type`, `status` and `path` (the record's path in the repository, with `/`). |\n| `active(root, type=None)` | A list of ids: the records whose frontmatter `status` is `ACTIVE` and that nothing supersedes. |\n| `edges(root, type=None, source=None, target=None)` | A list of `{\"type\", \"source\", \"target\"}`, one per edge that matches every filter given; each edge once. A dangling edge is included. |\n| `dangling(root)` | A list of `{\"type\", \"source\", \"target\"}`: every reference whose `target` is the id of no record. |\n| `commits(root, path=None)` | A list of `{\"commit\", \"task\", \"implements\"}`, one per commit of `HEAD`'s history, or per commit that changed `path`. `commit` is the full commit id; `task` and `implements` are lists of the ids in the commit's `Task:` and `Implements:` trailers. |\n\n`root` is a `pathlib.Path`. Every return value is plain JSON data (maps, lists, strings, numbers). The tests sort\nevery list themselves, so its order is not part of the interface. The store's tables are not part of the interface\neither: no test opens the database, beyond checking that the file is a SQLite database.\n\n", "chunk_id": "67fc18abf5b06e08805c72fe", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "de2d5a8efb718565180f7f83", "sha256": "2d97feae3aa537724a9fd420b891bc8cc34e092c42c22f0690f5b10d7f4b7d4d", "path": "tests/acceptance/W1-27/test_w1_27_rebuild.py", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 28, "text": "\"\"\"KPI success 2 and failure 2: ``gov rebuild`` recreates derived state.\n\nSuccess: rebuild recreates every derived store; two rebuilds give the same\ndigest; a fresh clone plus doctor plus rebuild works [CAP-07.a, CAP-20.a,\nCAP-46.a].\n\nFailure: rebuild needs anything not in git.\n\nRevised after implementation: rebuild goes through the lexical index's owner\nand its secrets filter (DEC-440); the fixture's size, not the behaviour,\nmade it time out.  Every case now uses a tiny project (~3 tracked files,\n~2\u20133 s per rebuild) with ``run_gov_with_code`` for the code root.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport shutil\n\nimport w1_27_support as support\nimport w2_67_codegraph\nimport w2_67_doctor\nimport w2_67b_support\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Command identity\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n", "chunk_id": "de2d5a8efb718565180f7f83", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "6b2fb1aff7df1532188f3444", "sha256": "190590216e7db8ab73cfa38921d7d99baae330e7779983a7d4e6feeb3c0da6a2", "path": "tests/acceptance/W2-69/test_w2_69_review_rebuild_root_and_held_store.py", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 49, "text": "the tool's home. Today the rebuild raises after building, exit 1 with a traceback,\nand leaves the code-graph store uncompacted.\n\nBehaviour 5: another process holds a SQLite store under ``.gov-runtime/`` during\n``gov rebuild --json``, so the rebuild cannot compact it: the rebuild names that\nstore, with the reason, on its standard error as well as in its JSON result. The\nheld store is the code-graph store, written by the stand-in tool, which starts the\nholding process (an exclusive lock, so no way of compacting gets through) before\nit returns: the code index is the rebuild's last store, so the store is held from\nits build to the end of the rebuild. Its exit code is not asked. Today the JSON\nresult alone names it.\n\nEvery rebuild is full (never ``--no-embeddings``): the semantic index is built\nagainst the first batch's stand-in embedder on a loopback port.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nimport w2_69_review_support as review\nimport w2_69_support as support\n\npytestmark = [support.needs_gitleaks, support.local_only]\n\nR = support.RUNTIME\nPAGES, KEPT = 24, 4\n", "chunk_id": "6b2fb1aff7df1532188f3444", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "d621f6adccea970c317bdb63", "sha256": "2a81993be0483851bd0e3889604af1185c74525ca8843d0df1dc668107cbfdbf", "path": "tests/acceptance/W2-69/test_w2_69_review_rebuild_root_and_held_store.py", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 18, "text": "\"\"\"W2-69, added after implementation from the review (DEC-136), behaviours 4 and 5: the rebuild's compaction step.\n\nKPI 3, success: \"Deleted text does not survive a rebuild: after a full rebuild,\ntext deleted from a SQLite store is in neither its rows nor its free pages ...\"\nFailure: \"Deleted text left in a store's free pages after a rebuild.\"\n\nBehaviour 4: ``gov rebuild --json`` given the project as a relative path (``--root\n.`` from the project's folder; the folder's name from its parent) returns its\nresult with exit 0 and compacts every SQLite store it builds, as it does with an\nabsolute path: no store is left with a free page. Each case rebuilds the project\nfirst by its absolute path, deletes most of its pages, and rebuilds it by the\nrelative path, so a store that is not compacted keeps free pages. The code-graph\nstore is the real tool's where ``codebase-memory-mcp`` is on ``PATH`` (as W1-16's\ncases: ``local_only``, it starts the tool's daemon, so the cases run alone);\nwithout it, a stand-in first on ``PATH`` writes a SQLite store with free pages in\nthe tool's home. Today the rebuild raises after building, exit 1 with a traceback,\nand leaves the code-graph store uncompacted.\n\n", "chunk_id": "d621f6adccea970c317bdb63", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "bac3f14cb5b2d611fc4345e6", "sha256": "64090bad5b9eeb7c51ea2436dec0516bf71d759b95efd635a6367333bcc86748", "path": "tests/unit/retrieval/test_w2_108_freshness_once.py", "start_line": 137, "end_line": 146, "text": "def test_a_store_rebuilt_is_seen(project):\n    root, counts, answers = project\n    answers()\n    (root / \".gov-runtime/store.db\").unlink()\n    assert answers()[2][\"status\"] == \"missing\" and answers()[3] == \"missing\"\n    assert semantic.refresh(root)[\"available\"] is True\n    _settle()\n    rebuilt = answers()\n    assert rebuilt[3] is None and rebuilt[0][\"hits\"] and rebuilt == _afresh(answers)\n    assert counts[\"tracked\"] >= 2 and counts[\"wanted\"] >= 2\n", "chunk_id": "bac3f14cb5b2d611fc4345e6", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "b16f5ae8963b520e85dae0a4", "sha256": "99b5aca6231d39bee4763f2b8dcdf7861e974af8d8f9a6eece83005cfe8c2200", "path": "tests/acceptance/W1-27/test_w1_27_rebuild_r4.py", "start_line": 203, "end_line": 241, "text": "def test_rebuild_stores_hold_no_secret(cli, rebuild_gov, rebuild_project, sandbox, interface):\n    \"\"\"``stores_with_secrets(root)`` returns nothing for a project after\n    ``gov rebuild`` \u2014 the same as after a plain refresh.  This is the\n    backstop the secrets-indexing family check of W1-15 uses.\n\n    KPI: \"rebuild recreates every derived store\" [CAP-07.a].\n    DEC-440: \"recreates the lexical index by the code that owns it\".\n\n    Currently fails: ``_preseed_lexical`` inserts the secret text into the\n    SQLite store's ``lexical_fts`` table; ``stores_with_secrets`` reads\n    the table rows and finds the secret there.\n\n    Revised after implementation: rebuild goes through the lexical index's\n    owner and its secrets filter (DEC-440); the fixture's size, not the\n    behaviour, made it time out.\n\n    Revised after implementation: the case imported the package into the\n    test process and passed only where PYTHONPATH was set.\n    \"\"\"\n    _project_with_secret(rebuild_project)\n\n    run = rebuild_gov(\"rebuild\", \"--json\")\n    support.assert_envelope(run, interface, command=\"rebuild\")\n    assert run.returncode == 0, f\"rebuild failed\\n{run.describe()}\"\n\n    snippet = (\n        \"import json, sys\\n\"\n        \"from pathlib import Path\\n\"\n        \"from gov.secrets import stores_with_secrets\\n\"\n        f\"tainted = stores_with_secrets(Path({str(rebuild_project)!r}))\\n\"\n        \"json.dump(tainted, sys.stdout)\\n\"\n    )\n    done = support.run_python_snippet(cli, sandbox, snippet)\n    assert done.returncode == 0, f\"stores_with_secrets snippet failed:\\n{done.stderr}\"\n    tainted = json.loads(done.stdout)\n    assert not tainted, (\n        f\"after rebuild, {len(tainted)} store(s) hold a secret: {tainted}\\n\"\n        f\"the secret bypassed the filter during rebuild\\n{run.describe()}\"\n    )\n", "chunk_id": "b16f5ae8963b520e85dae0a4", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "15666266334fd5ac8998ead6", "sha256": "d85674bd244d37df6bdc3badce8cac3a91d7f43823354c0ffa34743f09a5eae2", "path": "tests/acceptance/W1-27/test_w1_27_rebuild_r2.py", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 32, "text": "\"\"\"Round 2, KPI success 2: rebuild recreates every derived store.\n\nThe current ``src/gov/rebuild/command.py`` deletes ``store.db`` entirely\nand calls ``store_load``, which builds only the record graph (five tables).\nThe lexical index (W1-17) and semantic index (W1-19) tables are lost.\n\nEither rebuild recreates each derived store by calling the code that owns\nit, or it removes only what it can recreate and names what it left out.\n\nPredecessor analysis\n--------------------\nThe first round's ``test_w1_27_rebuild.py`` has five cases.  The closest\nis ``test_rebuild_recreates_derived_stores``, which only asserts that\n``.gov-runtime/`` **exists** \u2014 it never opens ``store.db`` to check\nwhich tables are present.  The predecessor's case was **weak**: it\nverified the directory, not the table set.\n\nRevised after implementation: rebuild goes through the lexical index's\nowner and its secrets filter (DEC-440); the fixture's size, not the\nbehaviour, made it time out.  Every case now uses a tiny project with\n``run_gov_with_code`` for the code root.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport sqlite3\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nimport w1_27_support as support\n", "chunk_id": "15666266334fd5ac8998ead6", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "fd19d357af90e6afc5908548", "sha256": "ce10f3dc5cda49f39f675395fcf54651161239b69f6b5e2d31c12334aab5bd34", "path": "tests/acceptance/W2-69/test_w2_69_deleted_text_after_rebuild.py", "start_line": 73, "end_line": 89, "text": "def test_after_a_full_rebuild_no_sqlite_store_has_a_free_page(sandbox, embedder):\n    project = support.make_rebuild_project(sandbox, _files())\n    env = support.rebuild_environment(sandbox, embedder, with_code_tool=False)\n    first = support.rebuild(project, env)\n    _assert_rebuilt(first, \"the first rebuild\")\n    stores = _sqlite_report(project)\n    assert f\"{R}/store.db\" in stores, f\"premise: the rebuild wrote the record store: {sorted(stores)}\"\n    assert all(count == 0 for count in stores.values()), f\"after the first rebuild, free pages: {stores}\"\n    for n in range(KEPT, PAGES):\n        (project / f\"docs/page{n:02d}.md\").unlink()\n    support.commit_all(project, \"most pages deleted\")\n    second = support.rebuild(project, env)\n    _assert_rebuilt(second, \"the rebuild after the deletion\")\n    stores = _sqlite_report(project)\n    assert all(count == 0 for count in stores.values()), (\n        f\"after a full rebuild that followed the deletion of {PAGES - KEPT} of {PAGES} pages, SQLite stores still \"\n        f\"hold free pages (not compacted): { {rel: n for rel, n in stores.items() if n} }\")\n", "chunk_id": "fd19d357af90e6afc5908548", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "8db91b1f59ed805d118fa824", "sha256": "6f8818fe2ab6c5886a26a83ca73f09150a9b2b26193973cc84d9880f3fcb501e", "path": "docs/research/W2-69-secrets-scan.md", "start_line": 317, "end_line": 329, "text": "## 12. The compaction step in the rebuild\n\n- **Where:** `src/gov/rebuild/command.py`, after each store's build.\n  - After `store_load`, `lexical_refresh` and `semantic_refresh`, which all write `.gov-runtime/store.db`: compact once, after the last of them (or after each).\n  - After `codeintel_index`: compact `.gov-runtime/codeintel/home/code.db` and `_config.db`.\n- **What, in order, on one connection:**\n  1. `INSERT INTO <fts>(<fts>) VALUES ('optimize')` for every FTS5 table in the store: `lexical_fts` in `store.db`, `nodes_fts` in `code.db`. Find them from `sqlite_master` (`sql LIKE 'CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE % USING fts5%'`), not from a fixed list.\n  2. `VACUUM`.\n- **`query-vector-cache.db`** is written by searches, not by the rebuild. It holds hashes and vectors, no text of a query. Compacting it in the rebuild costs nothing (20 KB) and keeps the backstop quiet. Recommended, but outside \"each store's build\".\n- **The record store's digest does not change.** It is taken over rows, not bytes, so two rebuilds from one commit keep one digest.\n- **If compaction fails,** for example a busy lock from the code-graph tool's daemon, the rebuild should report that store as not compacted. The backstop then fails closed on any text left in freed space.\n- **`PRAGMA secure_delete = ON`** in gov's own writers would make deletes zero their bytes on every build of SQLite, not only on this machine's. But it is outside this ticket's paths, and compaction already covers K3.\n\n", "chunk_id": "8db91b1f59ed805d118fa824", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "7dff0f60c20a12c5849218c2", "sha256": "493fc5093aebbce066bca84c5f6d0c0d21b3d02baf7db3680d8521592a61f637", "path": "tests/acceptance/W2-108/test_w2_108_change_seen.py", "start_line": 87, "end_line": 109, "text": "def test_a_store_rebuilt_by_another_process_is_seen(planted, driver, embedder, records):\n    \"\"\"The store rebuilt between two calls, by another process, with the tree and the head unchanged: a fully\n    rebuilt store, or one whose lexical index and vectors alone were refreshed (their own refresh functions).\"\"\"\n    S.write(planted, S.NEW_FILE, S.NEW_TEXT)\n    S.git(planted, \"add\", S.NEW_FILE)          # tracked, uncommitted: the head does not move (DEC-344)\n    stale = [S.lexical_freshness(), S.lexical_search(S.NEW_PHRASE), S.semantic_search(HERON_QUESTION)]\n    after = [S.lexical_freshness(), S.lexical_search(S.NEW_PHRASE), S.semantic_search(HERON_QUESTION),\n             S.retrieve(S.NEW_PHRASE)]\n    values = driver.run(planted, [*stale * 3, S.rebuild(records=records), *after], host=embedder.host).values()\n    before, later = values[:len(stale) * 3], values[len(stale) * 3:]\n    for number in range(0, len(before), len(stale)):\n        assert before[number] == {\"status\": S.STALE, \"stale\": [S.NEW_FILE]}, before[number]\n        assert S.facet(before[number + 1]) == (False, S.UNAVAILABLE, S.STALE), before[number + 1]\n        assert S.facet(before[number + 2]) == (False, S.UNAVAILABLE, S.STALE), before[number + 2]\n    freshness, lexical, semantic, bundle = later\n    assert freshness == {\"status\": S.FRESH, \"stale\": []}, \\\n        f\"the store was rebuilt by another process, but the old answer was reused: {freshness}\"\n    assert S.facet(lexical) == (True, S.AVAILABLE, None), lexical\n    assert [hit[\"path\"] for hit in lexical[\"hits\"]] == [S.NEW_FILE], lexical\n    assert S.facet(semantic) == (True, S.AVAILABLE, None), semantic\n    assert semantic[\"hits\"][0][\"path\"] == S.NEW_FILE, semantic[\"hits\"][:3]\n    assert bundle[\"facets\"][\"lexical\"][\"available\"] and bundle[\"facets\"][\"semantic\"][\"available\"], bundle[\"facets\"]\n    assert S.NEW_FILE in [item[\"path\"] for item in bundle[\"evidence\"]], bundle[\"evidence\"]\n", "chunk_id": "7dff0f60c20a12c5849218c2", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "b6c66c6a6a0ecea33da43286", "sha256": "17b496a5b5da2bcb89a81587623f3b92c1ecba99eabbfb4a265beda2a7c1fdf7", "path": "docs/research/W2-69-secrets-scan.md", "start_line": 133, "end_line": 144, "text": "## 6. The stores a rebuild writes\n\n| File | Writer | SQLite | Journal mode | `-wal`, `-shm`, `-journal` beside it | Size (bytes) | Page size | Pages | Free pages |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `.gov-runtime/store.db` | record store, lexical index, semantic store (`gov.store.load`, `gov.retrieval.lexical`, `gov.retrieval.semantic`) | yes | delete | none | 240,062,464 | 4,096 | 58,609 | 0 |\n| `.gov-runtime/codeintel/home/code.db` | the code-graph tool (codebase-memory-mcp, its own SQLite) | yes | delete | none | 92,405,760 | 65,536 | 1,410 | 8 |\n| `.gov-runtime/codeintel/home/_config.db` | the code-graph tool | yes | delete | none | 12,288 | 4,096 | 3 | 0 |\n| `.gov-runtime/query-vector-cache.db` | searches (`gov.retrieval.semantic`), not the rebuild | yes | delete | none | 20,480 | 4,096 | 5 | 0 |\n| 2,047 other files (21,801,978 bytes): code-index file copies, logs, `config.json`, records, snapshots, scratch | various | no | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\n| 6 placeholder device files | the sandbox | no (not regular files) | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\n\n- None of the stores uses WAL, and no `-wal`, `-shm` or `-journal` file was present after the lead's rebuild.\n", "chunk_id": "b6c66c6a6a0ecea33da43286", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "2ac5dc755745d4cb4f6e6138", "sha256": "a84818f30afcbebdf1d35c800088ff045c8628f60636860a40bb83893aaa0f2d", "path": "docs/research/W2-61-baseline.md", "start_line": 20, "end_line": 35, "text": "## 2. The stores' fingerprint\n\nThe clone's stores were built in the clone by the pinned gov: a bare `gov`, with no `PYTHONPATH` and no `GOV_TICKET` (DEC-877), as `flock /tmp/gov-os-rebuild.lock gov rebuild --json`, after the load and disk gates.\n\n| | Rebuild 1 | Rebuild 2 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Start and end (UTC) | 20:22:26 to 21:07:20 (44 min 54 s) | 22:03:02 to 22:10:15 (7 min 13 s) |\n| Gate at the start: disk; 1-, 5- and 15-minute load | 877 GiB and 64,915,633 inodes free; 10.15, 34.45, 53.93 | 873 GiB and 64,463,467 inodes free; 19.52, 32.33, 46.54 |\n| Exit code | 0 | 0 |\n| Stores (`lexical`, `semantic`, `codeintel`) | each `recreated` | each `recreated` |\n| Lexical timing (`timing.lexical_s`) | 141.8 s | 0.4 s |\n| Files compacted | `store.db`, `codeintel/home/_config.db`, `codeintel/home/code.db` | the same three and `query-vector-cache.db` |\n\n**The digest each rebuild records** (`result.digest` in `rebuild-1.json` and `rebuild-2.json`; `result.store.digest` is the same value, with no invalid entries):\n\n- the stores' fingerprint, rebuild 1's digest (`rebuild-1.json`): `5550b460ec6e3956ffa86f88f9217534cc6f12ffd37c39321be2d8cdea106e6c`\n", "chunk_id": "2ac5dc755745d4cb4f6e6138", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "b7ac62699615b1ea24326e11", "sha256": "394af7b50af97d72d37b9a362be7b3b28744b704e2708c187cbd81792af99f3b", "path": "tests/acceptance/W2-108/w2_108_support.py", "start_line": 454, "end_line": 456, "text": "def rebuild(semantic=True, records=True):\n    \"\"\"A step: another process rebuilds the store (see ``build_steps``).\"\"\"\n    return {\"op\": \"external\", \"steps\": build_steps(semantic, records)}\n", "chunk_id": "b7ac62699615b1ea24326e11", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "a5a7073b9fc80eb48840c52f", "sha256": "a2668b4496edddc50fa45cf6d26940204506482c378620cb890f8aa5acde85fc", "path": "tests/acceptance/W2-69/test_w2_69_deleted_text_after_rebuild.py", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 18, "text": "\"\"\"W2-69 (K3): deleted text does not survive a rebuild.\n\nSuccess: \"Deleted text does not survive a rebuild: after a full rebuild, text\ndeleted from a SQLite store is in neither its rows nor its free pages, so a secret\nremoved from the sources leaves no residue the check would find, or miss [DEC-897\nitem 1].\" It covers every SQLite store a rebuild writes: the record store with its\nlexical and semantic indexes, and the code-graph store the code-graph tool builds.\n\nFailure: \"Deleted text left in a store's free pages after a rebuild.\"\n\nEvery case runs ``gov rebuild --json`` (a full rebuild, never ``--no-embeddings``)\nin a temporary project of its own, with this worktree's code. The semantic index is\nbuilt against a stand-in embedder on a loopback port (vectors from a hash of each\ntext, 1,024 floats each, as the pinned model's), so it is rebuilt and its deleted\nvectors free pages, with no model and no network; the runner's user site is given\nto the rebuild so that ``sqlite_vec`` is found under the temporary HOME. The cases\nthat do not need the code-graph store hide the code-graph tool from PATH, so no\ndaemon starts and they can run beside other suites; the one case of the code-graph\n", "chunk_id": "a5a7073b9fc80eb48840c52f", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}, {"id": "97697aa677a19a4b740fe75b", "sha256": "36ac6e68e9c318755f6dcf29682f7735bb3062671bd74820ab13d315991dc703", "path": "tests/acceptance/W2-50/test_w2_50_never_indexed.py", "start_line": 95, "end_line": 123, "text": "def test_an_adopted_clone_in_the_own_folder_has_its_own_store_inside_it(indexed_project, sandbox):\n    \"\"\"The clone's rebuild makes the clone's store, inside the clone; the repository's stores do not change.\n\n    The repository's stores are compared without their ``logs`` folders: the\n    code index's daemon may still write its own log after the repository's\n    rebuild has returned, and a log is not an index.\n    \"\"\"\n    project = indexed_project\n    _rebuild(sandbox, project)\n    before = support.snapshot(project / \".gov-runtime\", skip_names=(\"logs\",))\n    clone = sandbox.own(MAIN) / \"clone\"\n    sandbox.own(MAIN).mkdir(parents=True)\n    support.git(sandbox.own(MAIN), \"clone\", \"-q\", \"--no-hardlinks\", str(project), str(clone))\n    support.write(clone / \"docs\" / \"clone-only.md\", f\"# Clone\\n\\nThe word {support.CLONE_MARKER} is in the clone.\\n\")\n    support.write(clone / \"docs\" / \"config.md\", f\"# Config\\n\\nThe value is {support.SECRET} today.\\n\")\n    support.git(clone, \"add\", \"-A\")\n    support.git(clone, \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"the clone's own work\")\n    _rebuild(sandbox, clone)\n\n    clone_store = clone / \".gov-runtime\"\n    assert support.holders(clone_store, support.CLONE_MARKER), (\n        f\"the clone's rebuild left no store of its own inside the clone ({clone_store})\")\n    assert support.snapshot(project / \".gov-runtime\", skip_names=(\"logs\",)) == before, (\n        \"the clone's rebuild changed this repository's stores\")\n    assert _store_files_holding(project, sandbox, support.CLONE_MARKER) == [], (\n        \"the clone's word reached this repository's stores or HOME outside the root\")\n    assert support.holders(clone_store, support.SECRET) == [], \"the planted secret reached the clone's own store\"\n    assert _store_files_holding(project, sandbox, support.SECRET) == [], (\n        \"a secret planted in the clone reached this repository's stores\")\n", "chunk_id": "97697aa677a19a4b740fe75b", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "W2-54-CIT-E", "sha256": "5483e2581829c514b35fcf9314f46a8843a33da90a35aee2baae82fd207ca2c5", "path": "docs/changes/W2-54-CIT-E.md", "start_line": 265, "end_line": 269, "text": "### 5.3 The five limits as built\n\n| Limit (DEC-782) | As built in `src/gov/retrieval/semantic.py` |\n|---|---|\n| 1. One derived file under `.gov-runtime/`, nothing authoritative | `.gov-runtime/query-vector-cache.db` (`QUERY_VECTORS_REL`), a SQLite file of its own: not `store.db`, not tracked (the runtime folder is ignored by git), read by no check and outside the store digest. Rollback-journal mode, never WAL, so no `-wal` or `-shm` file stays beside it; the journal exists only during a write and is removed at its commit or rollback. Nothing is written when the lexical or semantic index is missing, empty or stale (the search returns before the vector is asked for), as round 2. |\n", "chunk_id": "c356551096ded8dfd7e4d8c2", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "55acf8aaa1114cd27ef8d7b0", "sha256": "3fe46f44333a83d085e219d178c706b33f67f5580e8df86a52c8fe87d71865f5", "path": "tests/acceptance/W1-27/test_w1_27_rebuild_r2.py", "start_line": 132, "end_line": 137, "text": "\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n# Rebuild must report stores it could not recreate\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #\n\n", "chunk_id": "55acf8aaa1114cd27ef8d7b0", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "3fa08093eff0873296040f2c", "sha256": "07b34dab36d890048c9b33459f0edd011e674d1e558f710995b9dfab3f7ced2b", "path": "docs/assessment/2026-10/B-memory-retrieval.md", "start_line": 585, "end_line": 600, "text": "### F10. During a rebuild, reads fail with a wrong error code or a traceback\n\n**Evidence:**\n- **The probes.** During R1, at 12:53:\n  - `gov retrieve --json` gave `STORE_MISSING`, \"no record graph in the store \u2026 load it first\". `retrieve.py:49-50` maps any SQLite operational error, here \"database is locked\", to that code.\n  - `gov context --json` gave no envelope at all, only a 20-line Python traceback ending `sqlite3.OperationalError: database is locked` (`context/__init__.py:52`, from `_record_map`).\n- **The SessionStart hook** swallows that error (`sessionstart.py:121-129`), so a session that starts during a rebuild gets no brief and no warning.\n- **The cause:** the semantic build holds one write transaction across all embedding batches (`semantic.py:247-265`). R1 took 11 min 47 s.\n\nOrdinary work: yes, because DEC-719 asks for a full rebuild before each close and each planning or audit step, and any agent reading meanwhile hits it.\nConsequence: other\n\nA misleading error or a crash; nothing is written or lost.\n\n**Severity:** low-medium.\n\n", "chunk_id": "3fa08093eff0873296040f2c", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 2}, {"id": "75e5675a69a8758f464e2415", "sha256": "10eeb430248ce4afd113ef9e28da7afaca57cea30d0c82716ffe683c611139ae", "path": "docs/research/W2-69-secrets-scan.md", "start_line": 142, "end_line": 156, "text": "| 6 placeholder device files | the sandbox | no (not regular files) | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\n\n- None of the stores uses WAL, and no `-wal`, `-shm` or `-journal` file was present after the lead's rebuild.\n- The record store, the lexical index and the semantic store are one file (`store.db`).\n- The record store is rebuilt by `DROP TABLE` and `INSERT`. The lexical and semantic stores are updated in place (`DELETE` and `INSERT`).\n- The code-graph store is built anew after its folder is removed. But the tool deletes and rewrites rows while it builds.\n\nFreed space as built (the file-format parse in `residue.py`):\n\n| Store | Freelist pages: bytes / non-zero | Freeblocks: count / bytes / non-zero | Unallocated gaps: bytes / non-zero | Text-like runs (20+ word bytes) in freed space |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `store.db` | 0 / 0 | 2,176 / 218,379 / 0 | 5,377,995 / 87,971 | 159, on 153 pages |\n| `code.db` | 524,252 / 515,822 | 114 / 154,047 / 152,033 | 5,049,411 / 676,055 | 1,616 |\n| `_config.db`, `query-vector-cache.db` | 0 / 0 | 1 / 4 / 0 | about 10 to 12 KB / 0 | 0 |\n\n", "chunk_id": "75e5675a69a8758f464e2415", "routes": ["semantic"], "batch": 1}], "batches": [{"size": 10}, {"size": 10}], "merge": {"candidates": 20, "duplicates": 0, "dropped": [], "reranked": true}, "expansions": [{"chunk_id": "a5825dd584d1f9bcc50a5c99", "parent_id": "432c75e6a96d75598a75718c", "path": "docs/research/W2-87-memory-measure.md", "start_line": 38, "end_line": 66}, {"chunk_id": "67fc18abf5b06e08805c72fe", "parent_id": "98d7f0fff87f5b1bda1b9a8f", "path": "tests/acceptance/W1-10/README.md", "start_line": 31, "end_line": 57}, {"chunk_id": "b16f5ae8963b520e85dae0a4", "parent_id": "605707a6ef97359a4e2690ce", "path": "tests/acceptance/W1-27/test_w1_27_rebuild_r4.py", "start_line": 203, "end_line": 241}, {"chunk_id": "8db91b1f59ed805d118fa824", "parent_id": "4dfce9a4478f20fec68dd6cf", "path": "docs/research/W2-69-secrets-scan.md", "start_line": 317, "end_line": 329}, {"chunk_id": "7dff0f60c20a12c5849218c2", "parent_id": "2c9bb5f38b6f12d1f9870d91", "path": "tests/acceptance/W2-108/test_w2_108_change_seen.py", "start_line": 87, "end_line": 109}, {"chunk_id": "97697aa677a19a4b740fe75b", "parent_id": "18475f4acaea477f339a7525", "path": "tests/acceptance/W2-50/test_w2_50_never_indexed.py", "start_line": 95, "end_line": 123}], "gaps": [{"path": "tests/acceptance/W1-27/test_w1_27_recovery_check_r2.py", "chunk_id": "d33ce56b04be4f16fd83c8b3", "reason": "NOT_GATHERED"}, {"path": "docs/changes/W2-54-CIT-E.md", "chunk_id": "4b85346dee0d9c2dc3af5b5a", "reason": "NOT_GATHERED"}, {"path": "tests/acceptance/W1-30/test_w1_30_r11_rebuild_mode.py", "chunk_id": "7275fcc24a0b617b6ceb9635", "reason": "NOT_GATHERED"}, {"path": "docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/rebuild-a-dev-run7.json", "chunk_id": "f391395dc5fdba30acc0c716", "reason": "NOT_GATHERED"}, {"path": "tests/acceptance/W1-27/test_w1_27_rebuild_r5.py", "chunk_id": "26594cda8c959f44d8491e2b", "reason": "NOT_GATHERED"}, {"path": "tests/acceptance/W2-69/w2_69_support.py", "chunk_id": "3834d2ae314f2f92b6a2443c", "reason": "NOT_GATHERED"}, {"path": "docs/research/EXP-003/examin/README.md", "chunk_id": "721a25257284ed5fba35fc57", "reason": "NOT_GATHERED"}, {"path": "tests/acceptance/W1-27/test_w1_27_rebuild_r5.py", "chunk_id": "418dee426aae33aba3ffca31", "reason": "NOT_GATHERED"}, {"path": "docs/plan/wave-1-exit/evidence/gov-commands.json", "chunk_id": "9d47aab84188bf520196755c", "reason": "NOT_GATHERED"}, {"path": "tests/acceptance/W1-27/test_w1_27_rebuild.py", "chunk_id": "64a237ef048ef1d2751f8d34", "reason": "NOT_GATHERED"}], "facets": {"lexical": {"available": true, "reason": null}, "semantic": {"available": true, "reason": null}}, "budget": {"bundle": {"limit": 6000, "used": 5942}, "rounds": {"limit": 1, "used": 1}}, "continuation": "eyJiYiI6bnVsbCwiYnMiOjEwLCJpIjpbXSwibyI6MjAsInEiOiJob3cgZG9lcyBnb3YgcmVidWlsZCBjb3B5IG9yIHNlZWQgc3RvcmVzIGZyb20gYW5vdGhlciB0cmVlLCBzcWxpdGUgYmFja3VwIiwiciI6MCwidCI6bnVsbH0="}, "session": ""}
